  "about": "Frozen device evidence samples (D07-P06). The core challenge and serial number tests and the phone tests read this file. The challenge texts are hex, their SHA-256 digests hex; values, Secure Enclave keys, attestation objects and client data are base64url without padding, while the App Attest keyId keeps Apple's standard base64 with padding, as the identity contract takes it. Made up for these samples: the student numbers; the three verification values, the SHA-256 of \"iu-yoklama sample verification value N\" for N = 1, 2, 3; and the Secure Enclave key, a P-256 public key made once whose private half was never kept, so nothing can sign for it. Copied as they stand: the Android chains and the App Attest object, from the public test data of the open-source projects named in each source field (Apache-2.0, see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md next to this file). Each chain holds only between its validFrom and validTo; check it at its validAt, and its root note says whose root it reaches.",
